REST API in React
React + REST API = fetching data from a server and showing it in UI
In React, you implement REST API by calling API endpoints using fetch or Axios and displaying the data in UI.

REST API: Any API that uses REST principles, may follow some rules, may not strictly follow all 6 constraints
RESTful API: An API that strictly follows all REST constraints (rules)
REST API and RESTful API are similar, but RESTful API strictly follows all REST constraints, while REST API may not

React apps commonly use:
-> fetch() (built-in)
-> Axios (popular library)

